## Executive Summary

INC-001 was created following CORR-001 — Multi-Stage Windows Attack Activity.

The incident represented a controlled SOC lab simulation containing multiple suspicious Windows behaviors, including failed authentication, remote network authentication, PowerShell execution, scheduled-task activity, and privileged group modification.

The purpose of the investigation was to determine whether the individual detections formed a coherent attack sequence and to practice formal SOC incident investigation procedures.

The investigation determined that the security detections correctly identified intentionally generated suspicious activity.

The incident was therefore classified as:

```text
True Positive
Benign Positive — Authorized Security Testing
```

